  "Translation",
  "Translation and AI summary APIs. Supports a fallback provider chain that tries providers in priority order. Automatically switches to the next provider on failure. Each provider failure is classified by status code and response body (missing key, expired, forbidden, quota, billing, rate limit, server error, …) and returned as failures, which the editor shows as toasts. Providers that keep failing for the same reason are turned off and skipped, and each provider's usage is counted per month.",
  "Translations Cached One Row per Language",
  "Translations for viewing in another language are stored in content_translations, one row per (source type, source id, language). Source types are post and project details, labels inside bodies, site UI text bundles and list cards (posts, projects, series). A hash of the source is kept so unchanged text is never re-translated, and a partial result is saved with an empty hash so the next request fills only the gaps. Only the server (service_role) reads and writes it.",
